<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>RQ1: Gold-Switch Effectively Reduces Overthinking in LRMs</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2.2 Hard and Soft Superposition ‣ 3.2 Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition Between LRM and LLM ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 1</span></a>, <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3.2.2 Hard and Soft Superposition ‣ 3.2 Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition Between LRM and LLM ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> show the results of Gold-Switch on QwQ-32B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B, and Qwen3-4B, respectively.
Taking QwQ-32B as an example, on GSM8K, while QwQ-32B achieves higher accuracy compared with Qwen2.5-32B-Instruct, it takes almost 6× longer time to finish the same task.
By always turning on Gold-Switch, we can achieve almost the same speed while reducing the performance gap by 65%.
Meanwhile, switching on/off Gold-Switch further reduces the performance gap, though incurring a moderate time cost.
On ASDIV, we can observe a similar trend– the performance gap is almost similar, while the inference time is drastically reduced.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 2</span></a>shows the average token length of GSM8K and ASDIV on QwQ-32B. We can observe that always turning on Gold-Switch can significantly reduce the average token length, almost being similar to the base LLM Qwen2.5-32B-Instruct. More detailed statistics are provided in the Appendix.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When compared to an existing router-based solution RouteLLM, Gold-Switch achieves similar or better performance, while drastically decreasing the GPU memory usage. For example, on GSM8K, Gold-Switch improves the accuracy by 1.7-3.7% (<a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2.2 Hard and Soft Superposition ‣ 3.2 Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition Between LRM and LLM ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 1</span></a>,<a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3.2.2 Hard and Soft Superposition ‣ 3.2 Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition Between LRM and LLM ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>,<a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), while requiring similar or only 0.6× of time to finish (<a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2.2 Hard and Soft Superposition ‣ 3.2 Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition Between LRM and LLM ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">When compared to a prompt-based baseline NoThinking, while NoThinking often fails to decrease the generation time (<a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2.2 Hard and Soft Superposition ‣ 3.2 Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition Between LRM and LLM ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 1</span></a> and <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), Gold-Switch always succeeds to decrease the time drastically, up to 2.7× (<a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2.2 Hard and Soft Superposition ‣ 3.2 Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition Between LRM and LLM ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 1</span></a>).
Moreover, even when NoThinking is working exceptionally well, Gold-Switch can be combined with Nothinking to explore better performance (<a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3.2.2 Hard and Soft Superposition ‣ 3.2 Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition Between LRM and LLM ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, when compared to Qwen3-4B, which is trained to have slow- or fast- thinking switch, training-free superposition of Qwen3-4B-Thinking and Qwen3-4B-Instruct by Gold-Switch is much better– GSM8K accuracy is 1.9% higher, while ASDIV speed is 30% faster (<a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Gold-Switch: Training-Free Superposition of Slow- and Fast- Thinking LLMs" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
